[1m[38;5;231mWhere does the persistent person-identifying userId originate?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mServer issues it (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mlogin() returns the canonical user ID; client persists it for other forms. Trustworthy, but login() gains no userId
[39m     [38;5;246mparameter.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Person supplies it at login
     [38;5;246mAn external ID they already know, typed in and persisted. This is the reading where login(userId, ...) is correct.
[39m     [38;5;246mUnverified until the server confirms it.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Browser ID promoted at login
     [38;5;246mMint a visitor ID on first load, associate it with the real user after auth. Enables pre-login tracking; two IDs to
[39m     [38;5;246mmanage.[39m
